  "articleBody": "It's a common challenge to adapt a laundry room for accessibility, and you're not alone if you're feeling a bit lost. Many folks wonder what can actually be changed without tearing everything out. Good news: a lot can be done! We're talking about things like adjusting appliance height, widening doorways for easier access, and making sure controls are within reach for everyone. Think about where your storage is, too; often, moving shelves lower or opting for pull-out drawers can make a huge difference. Even the type of flooring matters – you want something safe and easy to navigate. Should you go with stacked units or front-loaders? That's a big question with different answers depending on your specific needs, but generally, front-load machines are a great starting point for accessibility. It's about creating a space that works for you, not against you, so you can do laundry comfortably and independently. Don't let the idea of a huge renovation stop you from making these important changes. There are many steps you can take to make your laundry room much more functional.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}